new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c7580c0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/PR.md
@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+# Coupon usage limits (total cap and one use per customer)
+
+Marketing wants to run limited coupons ("first 500 customers", "one per
+customer") without hand-editing the discount list when a promotion runs out.
+
+## Changes
+
+- New `shopcore.coupons` module:
+  - `CouponLimit(code, max_redemptions=None, once_per_customer=False)`.
+    `max_redemptions` is the total number of times a code can be redeemed
+    across all customers.
+  - `CouponRedemptions`: in-memory redemption counts per code and the set of
+    customers who used each code; `can_redeem(code, customer_id)`,
+    `record(code, customer_id)`, `redemptions(code)`.
+- `Order` gains an optional `customer_id`.
+- `PricingEngine` takes an optional `redemptions=` store:
+  - `eligible_discounts` drops entered codes that are no longer redeemable,
+    so a used-up code is quoted as if it had not been entered.
+  - New `record_redemptions(order, quote)`: checkout calls it once payment
+    has succeeded, with the quote that was paid, to count the redemption.
+    Quoting alone never consumes a code.
+
+## Notes
+
+- Codes are matched case-insensitively and trimmed, like coupon entry.
+- Guest orders (no `customer_id`) cannot use `once_per_customer` codes:
+  there is no way to tell two guests apart. This is intentional (agreed with
+  marketing).
+- Limits only apply to coupon codes customers enter; auto-applied
+  promotions are not coupons and are unaffected.
+- Persistence is out of scope; the store is in memory for now and will be
+  backed by the orders database in a follow-up.
+
+## Tests
+
+`tests/test_coupon_limits.py`: unlimited codes, once-per-customer, guests,
+quoting does not consume a code, config validation.
